---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<BaseLayout title="about" current="about">
  <article class="prose">
    <figure class="crest">
      <img src="/emblem.png" width="360" height="360" alt={`The ${site.name} maker's seal: a bearded pirate skull in a ship's wheel, over crossed cutlasses, above an "x-hakt" banner.`} />
    </figure>

    <h1 style="font-size:1.6rem;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin-bottom:1rem">about</h1>

    <p>
      {site.name}.com is one person writing down how a small mesh of servers is
      actually wired. Every note is a practitioner describing their own setup, with
      one diagram carrying the idea. If you came here looking for <em>how</em>, not
      <em>whether</em>, you are in the right place.
    </p>

    <p>
      The site is a sibling of <a href="https://control.x-hakt.com">Control Room</a>,
      the private dashboard that runs the same infrastructure. Same dark palette,
      same two typefaces, same restraint. The pirate streak is a maker's mark and a
      turn of phrase, never a costume the interface wears.
    </p>

    <h2>Colophon</h2>
    <p>
      Built with Astro and MDX, prerendered to static files, served behind Traefik
      on the same box it documents. Diagrams are drawn as SVG and reviewed by a
      human before they ship. Type is IBM Plex Mono and IBM Plex Sans.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .crest {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .crest img {
    width: 260px;
    height: auto;
    max-width: 60%;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .crest img { width: 180px; }
  }
</style>
